ADDITIONAL GRANT: CONTRIBUTIONS

PolyForm Strict permits no changes and no new works. Taken alone that would
also forbid contributing, since preparing a pull request requires copying the
repository and editing it.

The licensor therefore grants one narrow additional permission:

You may reproduce and modify the software solely to prepare and submit a
contribution back to this project, and for no other purpose.

That permission is limited in the following ways.

1. It covers preparing and submitting the contribution. It does not permit
   publishing, distributing, or running your modified copy for any other
   reason, and it does not permit keeping a modified copy in use after the
   contribution is submitted, declined, or abandoned.

2. It does not permit taking any part of this software into another project,
   whether or not that project is related to this one.

3. It ends if the contribution is declined, or if you stop pursuing it.

4. Submitting a contribution is subject to CONTRIBUTING.md, which sets out the
   terms on which contributions are accepted.

Nothing in this Additional Grant changes the PolyForm Strict License above in
any other respect.

